{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.QuantumSu2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.QuantumSu2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.FieldTheory.RatFunc.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt_two","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L74-L86","doc":"[2]_q = q + 1.\n\nProved through the *multiplicative relation* `q² − 1 = (q + 1)(q − 1)`\n(`div_eq_iff`) rather than by `field_simp`: the content is a\ndivision-free identity in `ℤ[q]`, and only the quotient presentation of\n`[n]_q` needs the field.  (§7c R[h] pattern; see the ground-ring note in\nthe module header for why `R_q = ℚ(q)` itself is not reducible here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L69-L72","doc":"[1]_q = 1 for all q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.qInt","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The q-integer [n]_q = (qⁿ - 1)/(q - 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv_right","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv_left","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L59-L59","doc":"K · K⁻¹ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.K_inv","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.K","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.F","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.E","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Generators E, F, K, K⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.instRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2.instRing","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/quantum-su2.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2.Algebra","@